<title>USA: NYSE seeks statement from Southern Union.</title>
<headline>NYSE seeks statement from Southern Union.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-09-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>The New York Stock Exchange said Tuesday it asked Southern Union Co to issue a public statement concerning unusual activity with the company's stock, but the company declined to comment.</p>
<p>The exchange said it sought the statement to indicate whether there were any corporate developments that could explain the activity.</p>
<p>Southern Union did not immediately return a telephone call from Reuters seeking comment.  </p>
<p>In trading Tuesday afternoon, the stock price was up 2-3/4 to 24.</p>
